    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 76.14 score, bolstered by a prime matchup against McDonald and a high probability for stolen bases due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery. We are also prioritizing **Mickey Moniak** (72.73) and **Brice Turang** (68.59). **Mickey Moniak** benefits immensely from a 14% park boost and a favorable platoon look, while **Brice Turang**\u2019s score is inflated by a generous matchup against the 4.92 xERA of Abbott, allowing his high-contact profile to thrive in the two-hole. **James Wood** remains a must-start at 63.21, as his elite .416 xwOBA and lead-off positioning provide a stable floor despite the threat of a tough southpaw.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages and park factors were the primary drivers for several mid-tier starts. **Seiya Suzuki** (61.19) gets a wind-aided boost, helping him clear the 60-point threshold alongside **Austin Riley**, who benefits from a favorable clash with McGreevy. We were tempted to activate **Edwin Arroyo**, but his 38.31 score fell short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Edwin Arroyo**\u2019s switch-hitting versatility is a asset, he was relegated to the bench due to a difficult matchup against the 3.67 xERA of Drohan and a suppressed batting order position.\n\nThe lineup remains focused on maximizing our scarcity-driven advantage in speed and efficiency, but we are monitoring the bottom of the order with caution. Both **Jose Caballero** and **Kyle Karros** are facing elite hold pitchers, which naturally drags down their viability; however, they remain in the lineup to preserve our game caps while we wait for higher-upside opportunities. We continue to manage the roster around the unavailability of **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Josh Naylor**, ensuring our active depth\u2014including reserves like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014is ready to plug gaps as the schedule progresses.",
